    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Transcription Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Speech-to-Text for this Python script. This simplifies the process of submitting audio for batch transcription. My next step will be to install and set up the Google Cloud Client Library to interface with their APIs.\n\n\n**Selecting Transcription Library**\n\nI've decided to proceed by implementing the Python script `submit_transcription.py`. I'll be leveraging the `google.cloud.speech` library for this integration, which will be essential for batch audio transcriptions. I need to ensure the implementation is compliant and identifiable for the provider. My focus is now on crafting the core Python code to submit the file.\n\n\n**Drafting Core Script**\n\nI'm now focused on writing the `submit_transcription.py` script. The plan is to use `google.cloud.speech` for batch submission, ensuring the code includes a placeholder for the audio file URI and comments to identify Google Cloud as the provider. I'm taking care to meet all requirements and will not introduce any additional files.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818078961,
          "start": 1789818075330
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b97878c2001Nj6viSYfWYSy1R",
      "message_id": "msg_0b97873a3001Gyzs5oVfK55qk0",
      "session_id": "ses_f46878ceeffeDsLMsBuUnEd3J1",
      "time_created": 1789818075330,
      "time_updated": 1789818078962
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "1rvhxjYE4BQs4Sx9",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import speech_v1p1beta1 as speech\n\ndef submit_transcription(gcs_uri: str):\n    \"\"\"Submits an audio file for batch transcription using Google Cloud Speech-to-Text.\n\n    Args:\n        gcs_uri: The Google Cloud Storage URI of the audio file to transcribe.\n                 Example: \"gs://cloud-samples-data/speech/brooklyn_bridge.flac\"\n    \"\"\"\n\n    client = speech.SpeechClient()\n\n    audio = speech.RecognitionAudio(uri=gcs_uri)\n    config = speech.RecognitionConfig(\n        encoding=speech.RecognitionConfig.AudioEncoding.FLAC,\n        sample_rate_hertz=16000,\n        language_code=\"en-US\",\n        # Use a model adapted for long-form audio for batch transcription\n        model=\"default\",\n    )\n\n    operation = client.long_running_recognize(config=config, audio=audio)\n\n    print(\"Waiting for operation to complete...\")\n    response = operation.result(timeout=90)\n\n    # The result is an iteration of transcriptions. In a real application,\n    # you would process these results further.\n    for result in response.results:\n        print(f\"Transcript: {result.alternatives[0].transcript}\")\n        print(f\"Confidence: {result.alternatives[0].confidence}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Replace with your actual GCS URI\n    # This is an example from Google Cloud Speech-to-Text documentation\n    # For this to work, you need to have a Google Cloud project set up\n    # and authenticated (e.g., via `gcloud auth application-default login`)\n    # and the service account needs permissions to read from the GCS bucket\n    # and use the Speech-to-Text API.\n    example_gcs_uri = \"gs://cloud-samples-data/speech/brooklyn_bridge.flac\"\n    submit_transcription(example_gcs_uri)\n",
            "filePath": "submit_transcription.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
